        "original_id": "0e9d5aac-a9e1-527d-8e59-417a3746cbe6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: HNoMS Draug\n- Organizations: Royal Norwegian Navy\n- Concepts: Draugr, Norse mythology\n\nFacts:\n- Two ships of the Royal Norwegian Navy have borne the name HNoMS \"Draug\".\n- HNoMS \"Draug\" was named after the sea revenant Draugr.\n- The draugr, also called draug or aptrganga/aptrgangr, is an undead creature from Norse mythology.\n- The term aptrganga or aptrgangr literally means \"again-walker\".\n- The draugr is called \"draugur\" in modern Icelandic, \"dreygur\" in Faroese, and \"draug\" in Danish, Swedish, and Norwegian.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
